ot alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u11.2603\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u15.4022\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u16.4063\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u17.4359\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u18.4879\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u19.5230\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u23.7007\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u24.7186\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u25.7275\"},{\"reason\":\"The remaining units concern headings, signatures, monitoring, disclosure context, or dealing-frequency controls and do not alter the selected exception-attachment reading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u26.7393\"},{\"reason\":\"Provides disclosure authority and context, without changing the selected exception.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u27.7511\"}],\"dimensions\":[{\"dimension\":\"scope\",\"explanation\":\"The strongest reading covers a specific product or a particular product type, including linked fund types or fund houses, when a distributor promotes to a client. A narrower named-product-only reading is possible only by disregarding the express product-type language.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"definitions\",\"explanation\":\"A guaranteed return is typically composed of the underlying fund return and a distributor top-up. The source does not itself classify every component as a gift; gift and discount status require offer-specific judgment.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u7.1360\",\"db43e253bea18.u12.2646\",\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"exceptions\",\"explanation\":\"The fee or charge discount exception attaches to the gift prohibition. It does not, on the supplied text, immunise a distinct non-discount gift or top-up bundled with a discount.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"modality\",\"explanation\":\"The operative rule is ‘should not offer’; the circular separately says returns or incentives may be considered gifts. This is a conduct restriction, not the section 103 offence.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u12.2646\",\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\",\"db43e253bea18.u9.1940\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"time\",\"explanation\":\"The control applies when the distributor promotes the product or product type to a client. No commencement, deadline, or transition rule is supplied.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"dependencies\",\"explanation\":\"The FAQ answer referenced by footnote 3 and the complete Code provisions remain necessary to resolve classification boundaries; section 103 and advertising rules are separate dependencies.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u28.7987\",\"db43e253bea18.u29.8110\",\"db43e253bea18.u30.8235\",\"db43e253bea18.u9.1940\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"}],\"questions\":[\"Is each offered benefit separately identifiable, and what evidence supports classifying it as a gift, fee/charge discount, fund return, or distributor top-up?\",\"Does the referenced FAQ answer add a rule for gifts linked to fund types or fund houses?\",\"What effective version and commencement date govern the Code provision?\",\"Are any accompanying representations misleading or deposit-like under the separate advertising controls?\",\"Does the offer separately trigger section 103, independent of the gift restriction?\"],\"readings\":[{\"assumptions\":[\"The selected offer has a finite, separately identifiable component inventory.\",\"Unknown classifications remain unknown.\",\"This is an interpretation proposal, not a legal determination.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u0.2\"},{\"quote\":\"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u12.2646\"},{\"quote\":\"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"},{\"quote\":\"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"}],\"distinction\":\"The exception is component-specific: a fee or charge discount is excluded from the gift prohibition, while a distinct non-discount gift remains caught. Product-type promotion is expressly included. A guaranteed return is not automatically a gift; classification is required.\",\"family\":\"exceptions\",\"formalization\":{\"facts\":[{\"meaning\":\"The selected actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds.\",\"name\":\"actor_is_distributor\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u0.2\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean\"},{\"meaning\":\"The offer promotes a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.\",\"name\":\"promotion_scope_satisfied\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean\"},{\"meaning\":\"At least one separately identifiable offered component is a gift and is not a discount of fees or charges.\",\"name\":\"non_discount_gift_component\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"db43e253bea18.u12.2646\",\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean\"}],\"result\":\"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_scope_satisfied non_discount_gift_component)\",\"result_type\":\"bool\",\"scope\":\"(and actor_is_distributor promotion_scope_satisfied)\"},\"local_id\":\"component_specific_exception\",\"questions\":[\"How should an inseparable combined benefit be classified?\",\"What evidence establishes that a benefit is a fee or charge discount rather than another incentive?\"],\"statement\":\"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] True means the selected distributor offer is within the client/product-or-type scope and contains a non-discount gift component caught by the quoted should-not-offer rule. False means at least one required condition is established absent; it does not establish whole-firm compliance or resolve section 103.\",\"subject\":\"Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction for one promotional offer\"},{\"assumptions\":[\"The offer is assessed as one indivisible package.\",\"The package is treated according to its dominant or principal economic character, if such a character can be established.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges)\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u13.2987\"},{\"quote\":\"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.\",\"unit_id\":\"db43e253bea18.u12.2646\"}],\"distinction\":\"A competing reading treats the exception as applying to the combined package when its principal character is a fee or charge discount. The supplied text does not provide a dominance or inseparability test, so this reading is materially less supported and cannot be operationalised without additional authority.\",\"family\":\"exceptions\",\"formalization\":null,\"local_id\":\"package_level_exception\",\"questions\":[\"Does the referenced FAQ or full Code specify how bundled or inseparable benefits are classified?\",\"Can the package be decomposed economically and contractually?\"],\"statement\":\"The source leaves unresolved whether a genuinely inseparable package containing a discount and another benefit is assessed component-by-component or as a whole package.\",\"subject\":\"Alternative attachment of the fee/charge discount exception\"}]}"}}
